I've finally been able to get the nethack level compiler to work
with Xenix/286.  The fix is simple: generate the lexer with flex
rather than lex.

There seems to be a bug in the lexical analyser generated by lex.
Since I got around the problem, I'm not likely to investigate it
further.

If any of you are still having trouble compiling nethack on a '286,
drop me a line and I'll see how I can help.

